hash ae3731358decff37
note One frame: the elapsed time, the script's next lines, the app's frame, the Renderer presenting its DrawList, the cursor, and then the Input is cleared of everything that was momentary. The frame is timed here and the count, the worst and how many went over 16 ms accumulate on the runner, which is the only measurement of smoothness the tool has. Whatever the frame asked for becomes the next redraw deadline (a script instead runs a frame every 8 ms), and a frame or a script that asked to quit exits the loop.

